{"kind":"stack","id":"s-light-reflect","title":"Light reflects off surfaces","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Reflection"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"When light bounces off a surface and changes direction."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"What happens to light when it hits a shiny mirror?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"It bounces back","why":"Mirrors reflect light, so the light bounces back.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"It soaks into the glass","why":"Pupils may think shiny things absorb light like dark things do.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"It stops completely","why":"Pupils may think light disappears when it reaches a surface.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which surface reflects light the best?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A smooth mirror","why":"Smooth shiny surfaces reflect light most clearly.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A rough wooden block","why":"Pupils may think any solid object reflects light equally well.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A black cloth","why":"Pupils may think dark surfaces reflect light because they are visible.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"castle"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Your torch beam is lost in a dark cave. Do you aim it at a shiny wall or a dull rock?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Shiny wall","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Dull rock","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"The shiny wall bounces the light back and shows you the way out. Well done!"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The dull rock soaks up most of the light, so the cave stays dim. Try again next time."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Smooth surface"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-e","content":"A flat, even surface that reflects light in a clear, regular way."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"What do we call light that bounces off a surface?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Reflected light","why":"Light that bounces off a surface is called reflected light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Absorbed light","why":"Pupils may confuse absorbed light, which is taken in, with light that bounces back.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Hidden light","why":"Pupils may think light vanishes or hides when it meets a surface.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which of these helps you see yourself in a puddle?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Light reflecting off the water","why":"The still water reflects light back to your eyes, showing your image.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Light made by the water","why":"Pupils may think water produces its own light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Light sinking into the water","why":"Pupils may think light disappears into water instead of bouncing back.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"How many times can one ray of light reflect off a flat mirror?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"One","why":"A single reflection happens when light bounces once off the mirror.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Zero","why":"Pupils may think light cannot bounce at all off a mirror.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Ten","why":"Pupils may think light keeps bouncing many times, like an echo.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"Why can you see your face in a mirror?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Light reflects off your face into the mirror and back to your eyes","why":"Light bounces off you, hits the mirror, and reflects back to your eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"The mirror makes its own picture of you","why":"Pupils may think the mirror creates the image rather than reflecting light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"Your eyes send light out to the mirror","why":"Pupils may think eyes give out light, like a torch.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"You finished the light reflection lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"Great work noticing how light bounces off surfaces. Keep looking for reflections around you."}],"actions":[]}}
